On Tue, 21 May 2002 axp-kernel-list-request@redhat.com wrote:

On the Alphaserver 2000, i have found that upgrading to the 
latest firmware is a MUST. Could you provide me with some
kind of log to see how far you get?. BTW, should your system
be a 2100A or some kind of hybrid system (Like a 2100A in a
2000/2100 enclosure), you are out of luck with all free OS's 
except FreeBSD, as none of them supports the Lynx architecture.

Anyways, it is possible to run Linux or some of the BSD's on
most configurations, so there a big chance that one will work
for you. One caveat is that the EISA Mylex DAC960 is not
supported in Linux nor FreeBSD, but you can replace it with
any PCI based DAC 960 (Out of a PeeCee) with 2.73 firmware (FreeBSD
only) or 3.x firmware (Linux/FreeBSD). 

Provide me detailed specs on your system (Especcialy on the disk
subsystem) to help you further. 

Regards
Roberto de Iriarte
roberto@spock.cl

(Pleace cc me any answer as i receive the list on a digest basis
to answer you faster!)

